DS3D video databridge is an implementation of `ds3d::databridge` which connects
a standard DeepStream 2D video pipeline to a DS3D 3D pipeline. It takes the
`NvBufSurface` and `NvDsBatchMeta` of an incoming video batch and exposes them
as 2D frames and object metadata inside a `ds3d::datamap`, so a 3D filter can
consume camera images and 2D detections alongside LiDAR data.

Unlike the other DS3D modules this one does depend on GStreamer, because it
reads DeepStream video buffers and batch metadata directly.

`libnvds_3d_video_databridge.so` is built from these source files. and the video
databridge is created through API `createVideoBridge2d3d`. Application users can
call this API to instantiate this databridge.

The config content shall as:

    type: ds3d::databridge
    out_caps: ds3d/datamap
    custom_lib_path: libnvds_3d_video_databridge.so
    custom_create_function: createVideoBridge2d3d
    config_body:
       ...

Any custom `ds3d::databridge` must derive from `ds3d::BaseImplDataBridge` for data bridging
And implement the following interfaces:

    ErrCode startImpl(const std::string& content, const std::string& path) override;
    ErrCode processImpl(
        const struct VideoBridge2dInput* inputData, OnGuardDataCBImpl outputDataCb,
        OnGuardBridgeDataCBImpl inputConsumedCb) override;
    ErrCode stopImpl() override;
    ErrCode flushImpl() override;

In addition, users also need export a C-API for application to intiate this databridge.
The exported C-API name is not limited. In this sample, it is `createVideoBridge2d3d`.

More details, refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for section of "DeepStream 3D Custom Manual".
https://nvidia-deepstream.docs.buildwithfern.com/deepstream/9.2/text/DS_3D_Custom_Manual

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- libnvds_3d_common.so (build and install ds3d/common first)
- libgstreamer1.0 Development package
- libyaml-cpp Development package
- CUDA Runtime

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing this `ds3d::databridge` lib:
- Export CUDA_VER, then build. sudo -E keeps the variable for make.
  $ export CUDA_VER=13.2 # x86, Jetson and SBSA. For IGX Thor, CUDA_VER=13.0
  $ make && sudo -E make install
- Verify `libnvds_3d_video_databridge.so` exist and installed well.

NOTE: Compiling does not need root. Install with `sudo -E` so CUDA_VER is kept. Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).
